WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:00.330 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  what was once a thick-walled built to  protect one of Hungary's grandest  castles  has been transformed into a lookout with  the most beautiful and panoramic views  of Budapest  [Music]  the fisherman's bastion is a 500 foot  long lookout located on the bank of the  Danube River and is one of the most  visited sites in all of Budapest the  site is only around 100 years old and  was built in celebration of the 1000th  birthday of the Hungarian state the near  Romanesque medieval style architecture  reflects the era of the first Hungarian  King ruled in the year 1000 the bastions  most distinguishing features are the  seven turrets representing the seven  Hungarian tribes who founded the  present-day country in the year 895 the  name fisherman's bastion honors the  guild of fishermen who protected the  castle from being destroyed during the  Middle Ages from enemies the intention  in its construction was to create a  landmark that would showcase Budapest  it's gorgeous views their success is  evident as fisherman's bastion archways  windows and wide Comino stairways  provide a view unlike any other in all  of Budapest  [Music]

